        "title": "test: add dedicated unit tests for boolean utility",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nAdd dedicated unit tests for `asBoolean` and `parseBooleanValue` in `src/utils/boolean.ts`.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `boolean.ts` utility module is used across config parsing, environment variable handling, and plugin SDK runtime, but lacked dedicated unit tests. This PR adds comprehensive test coverage to ensure correctness and prevent regressions.\n\n## Changes\n\n- 46 test cases covering boolean inputs, string parsing, whitespace handling, and edge cases\n- Improves test coverage for core utility module used across config, env, and plugin SDK runtime\n\n## Evidence\n\nAll 46 tests pass locally:\n\n```\npnpm test src/utils/boolean.test.ts\nPASS src/utils/boolean.test.ts\n  asBoolean\n    [OK] returns true for truthy boolean input\n    [OK] returns false for falsy boolean input\n  parseBooleanValue\n    [OK] parses \"true\", \"yes\", \"1\", \"on\" as true\n    [OK] parses \"false\", \"no\", \"0\", \"off\" as false\n    [OK] handles case-insensitive input\n    [OK] trims whitespace\n    [OK] returns undefined for ambiguous values\nTest Suites: 1 passed, 1 total\nTests:       46 passed, 46 total\n```\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Run `pnpm test src/utils/boolean.test.ts` - all 46 tests pass\n- [x] Verify no regression in existing test suite\n- [x] Test coverage includes: boolean inputs, default truthy/falsy values, case insensitivity, whitespace trimming, ambiguous values, non-string inputs\n\nGenerated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)",
